    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version of the monologue:\n\n\"I'm tired of feeling like the more you protest, the more you blow your top, the more the system digs in its heels, and the more people like me are labeled as 'looters' or 'mis guided'. The establishment doesn't seem to care about the specifics of what's plaguing regular families - the crippling costs of healthcare, housing, and education; the literal fights to just make ends meet in middle-class America - but instead they prop up the indignities of trickle-down theories that only serve to make the whole thing worse. The mainstream media seems hell-bent on demonizing anyone who dares to question the 'experts', instead of showcasing the stand-up politicians who can actually speak to the needs of working people. It's like we're not even on the map, and the ones who truly matter are invisible to them. That's what's broken right now: the entire network of 'experts' and talking heads and elite received wisdom that's perpetuated by the noise networks and glossy media to create the illusion that everything is fine when, in reality, our basic lives are falling apart.\"",
